Feature: Sales Data Processing

  Scenario: Happy Path - Successful Data Ingestion and Storage
    Given the sales data file "sample_sales_data.csv" is available
    When the data is ingested into the Unity Catalog schema "purgo_playground"
    Then the data must be successfully stored with correct data types:
      | Field       | Data Type |
      | country_cd  | STRING    |
      | product_id  | STRING    |
      | qty_sold    | INTEGER   |
      | sales_date  | DATE      |

  Scenario: Validation - Incorrect Data Format
    Given the sales data file contains "qty_sold" with values in a non-numeric format
    When an attempt is made to ingest the data
    Then the process should fail with the error message "Invalid data format for 'qty_sold'. Expected INTEGER."

  Scenario: Validation - Future Date in Sales Date
    Given the sales data file contains "sales_date" in the future
    When an attempt is made to ingest the data
    Then the process should fail with the error message "Sales date cannot be in the future."

  Scenario Outline: Data Transformation and Preprocessing
    Given the sales data file with entries <qty_sold> and <sales_date>
    When preprocessing for <country_cd> and <product_id>
    Then the data should be transformed to match required analysis format
      | qty_sold_transformed | sales_date_transformed |
    Where:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  | qty_sold_transformed | sales_date_transformed |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  | 50                   | 20240115               |
      | UK         | P1002      | 30       | 2024-01-16  | 30                   | 20240116               |

  Scenario: Security and Compliance Adherence
    Given the sales data is ingested into the catalog
    When accessing the data
    Then ensure data is encrypted at rest and in transit
    And comply with relevant data protection regulations

  Scenario: Error Handling - Database Connectivity
    Given the database connection is not established
    When an attempt is made to ingest data
    Then the process should abort with the error message "Failed to connect to database. Check your network connection."

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog schema "purgo_playground" is created and accessible

  Examples:
    | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |
    | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  |
    | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17  |
    | IN         | P1001      | 60       | 2024-01-20  |
    | AU         | P1004      | 55       | 2024-01-22  |